confirmed,FRT-20260111-0728,,Department of Health and Human Services,HHS,Centers for Disease Control and Prevention,,BENEFITS,facial_recognition,biometric,PRA_ONLY,False,False,True,,,"The Laboratory Response Network is an integrated national and international network of laboratories that can respond to suspected acts of biological, chemical, or radiological terrorism and other public health emergencies.   Member laboratories submit information regarding the testing capabilities of the laboratory; report all biological and chemical testing results; and participate in Proficiency Testing Challenges or Validation. The goal of the study is to identify gaps in preparedness for bio",,,https://www.reginfo.gov/public/do/PRASearch?icRef=0920-0850,,,201902-0920-020,0920-0850,,,,
